_⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🔴 Critical_

**Cleanup function is never used and filter parsing is naive.**

Two critical issues:

1. **Unused cleanup**: The cleanup function returned by `applyVisionFilter` (lines 24-26) is never captured or used. Line 29 calls `applyVisionFilter()` without storing its return value, so filters won't be properly restored when `vision` changes or the component unmounts.

2. **Naive parsing**: Line 13 splits `document.body.style.filter` by space, which breaks if existing filters contain spaces (e.g., `drop-shadow(2px 2px 4px black)` would be split incorrectly).



<details>
<summary>🔎 Proposed fix</summary>

```diff
-  const applyVisionFilter = useCallback(() => {
+  const applyVisionFilter = useCallback((previousFilter?: string) => {
+    const savedFilter = previousFilter ?? document.body.style.filter;
     const existingFilters = document.body.style.filter.split(' ').filter((filter) => {
       return filter && filter !== 'none' && !knownFilters.includes(filter);
     });

     const visionFilter = filters[vision as keyof typeof filters]?.filter;
     if (visionFilter && document.body.classList.contains('sb-show-main')) {
       document.body.style.filter = [...existingFilters, visionFilter].join(' ');
     } else {
       document.body.style.filter = existingFilters.join(' ');
     }
-
-    return () => {
-      document.body.style.filter = existingFilters.join(' ');
-    };
+    return savedFilter;
   }, [vision]);

-  useEffect(applyVisionFilter, [vision]);
+  useEffect(() => {
+    const savedFilter = applyVisionFilter();
+    return () => {
+      document.body.style.filter = savedFilter;
+    };
+  }, [applyVisionFilter]);
```

For the parsing issue, consider using a more robust approach to preserve complex filters, such as tracking the original filter value before any modifications or using a CSS parser library.
</details>

<!-- suggestion_start -->

<details>
<summary>📝 Committable suggestion</summary>

> ‼️ **IMPORTANT**
> Carefully review the code before committing. Ensure that it accurately replaces the highlighted code, contains no missing lines, and has no issues with indentation. Thoroughly test & benchmark the code to ensure it meets the requirements.

```suggestion
  const applyVisionFilter = useCallback((previousFilter?: string) => {
    const savedFilter = previousFilter ?? document.body.style.filter;
    const existingFilters = document.body.style.filter.split(' ').filter((filter) => {
      return filter && filter !== 'none' && !knownFilters.includes(filter);
    });

    const visionFilter = filters[vision as keyof typeof filters]?.filter;
    if (visionFilter && document.body.classList.contains('sb-show-main')) {
      document.body.style.filter = [...existingFilters, visionFilter].join(' ');
    } else {
      document.body.style.filter = existingFilters.join(' ');
    }

    return savedFilter;
  }, [vision]);

  useEffect(() => {
    const savedFilter = applyVisionFilter();
    return () => {
      document.body.style.filter = savedFilter;
    };
  }, [applyVisionFilter]);
```

</details>

<!-- suggestion_end -->

<details>
<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>

```
In code/addons/a11y/src/withVisionSimulator.ts around lines 12 to 29, the
cleanup returned by applyVisionFilter is never used and the filter parsing is
brittle; fix by capturing the original document.body.style.filter (as a single
string, defaulting to empty) before any changes instead of splitting by spaces,
then in the effect call applyVisionFilter and return its cleanup so the original
filter is restored on vision changes/unmount, and when applying the vision
filter concatenate the original filter and the new vision filter with a single
space only when the original is non-empty, while still ensuring you only apply
when document.body.classList.contains('sb-show-main').
```

</details>

